@* PF-2837: the WUI Zone map legend, opened from the question mark icon in the layer control. Showing and
   hiding is pure CSS, so it needs nothing beyond the markup MapLayerLegendHelpers puts in the layer name, and
   it closes on its own when the pointer leaves the control and Leaflet collapses it. *@
<style type="text/css">
    .map-layer-legend-wrapper { position: relative; }

    /* Color, cursor and spacing come from the theme's .helpicon, the same as the field definition help icon,
       so this only strips the button chrome. A little smaller than that icon's 18px to sit better against the
       layer labels around it. Scoped to the layer control to outweigh .helpicon's own font-size regardless of
       stylesheet order. */
    .leaflet-control-layers .map-layer-legend-icon {
        padding: 0;
        background-color: transparent;
        border: none;
        font-size: 16px;
        line-height: 1;
        vertical-align: middle;
    }

    .map-layer-legend {
        display: none;
        position: absolute;
        left: 100%;
        top: -5px;
        margin-left: 8px;
        z-index: 1200;
        padding: 5px 7px;
        background-color: #F5F5F5;
        border: 1px solid #84AFD3;
        border-radius: 3px;
        box-shadow: 0 2px 6px rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.25);
        font-size: 11px;
        line-height: 15px;
        font-weight: normal;
        text-align: left;
        white-space: nowrap;
    }

    /* Kept open while the pointer is on the legend itself so it can be read without it vanishing. */
    .map-layer-legend-icon:hover + .map-layer-legend,
    .map-layer-legend-icon:focus + .map-layer-legend,
    .map-layer-legend:hover {
        display: block;
    }

    .map-layer-legend-row { display: block; }

    .map-layer-legend-swatch {
        display: inline-block;
        width: 12px;
        height: 12px;
        margin-right: 5px;
        vertical-align: middle;
        border: 1px solid #999999;
    }
</style>
